pack: vianney-en
version: 1
language: en
note: Draft starter pack from the project; the questions, word lists and lexicon weights are drafts that the rule author should correct, and the weights are placeholder tiers (0.95, 0.75, 0.50, 0.15) to be calibrated later on a labelled set.

# DEFAULT SENSITIVITY POLICY. For rules whose cue words also occur in reverent or educational speech
# (the Lord's name, oaths, blasphemy, renunciation, curses, calumny) the default "flag at" is above the 0.75
# tier: from word lists alone only the unambiguous 0.95-tier cues flag, and the 0.75 tier waits for the
# on-device AI or for you to move the slider down. Wrongly hiding a sermon costs more than missing a cue.

# Every rule below is traced to verbatim passages of the Curé d'Ars, quoted with their sources on the rules page
# of the project site (rules.md in the repository).
# Ten rules are enabled by default (the tongue, detraction and calumny, impure words and sights).
# The other twenty are broad or over-flagging and ship disabled: see "Notes on defaults" on that page.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The tongue: the six categories of the second Commandment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

rule lords_name
  title: Taking the Lord's name in vain
  source: Sur le deuxième Commandement
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: lords_name_strong, lords_name_bare
  ask noul: Is the name of God, Jesus or Christ used here as an exclamation or a curse, and not in prayer, worship, quotation or talk about religion?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=hide, watch-meta=warn-overlay, subtitles=mute-word
  enabled: true

rule oaths
  title: Oaths, calling God to witness
  source: Sur le deuxième Commandement
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: oath_cues
  ask noul: Does the speaker swear by God or by something sacred to vouch for a claim or promise (for example 'I swear to God', 'so help me God'), and not as a formal oath in court, a wedding vow or a prayer?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=warn-overlay, subtitles=mute-word
  enabled: true

rule blasphemy
  title: Blasphemy
  source: Sur le deuxième Commandement
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: blasphemy_terms
  ask noul: Is God, Jesus, the Virgin Mary or a saint insulted or mocked here (for example called cruel, unjust or powerless), and not just quoted, discussed or prayed to?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=hide, watch-meta=warn-overlay, subtitles=mute-word
  enabled: true

rule renunciation
  title: Renouncing God in anger
  source: Sur le deuxième Commandement
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: renunciation_cues
  ask noul: Does the speaker rage against God or disown Him in anger over a loss or misfortune (for example 'God has abandoned me', 'to hell with God'), and not calmly explain why he does not believe?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.85
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=warn-overlay, subtitles=mute-word
  enabled: true

rule curses_imprecations
  title: Curses and imprecations
  source: Sur le deuxième Commandement
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: curses_imprecations
  ask noul: Does the speaker, in anger or despair, call down harm, damnation or death on a person, an animal, a thing or himself (for example 'damn you', 'I hope you die', 'may I be struck dead if I lie'), and not in a joke, a story or a quoted lyric?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=hide, watch-meta=warn-overlay, subtitles=mute-word
  enabled: true

rule coarse_words
  title: Coarse words
  source: Sur la Pénitence
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: coarse_words
  ask noul: Is a vulgar or obscene word used here crudely, and not as a medical or educational term, a place name or a quotation under discussion?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.70
  action: feed-card=hide, watch-meta=warn-overlay, subtitles=mute-word
  enabled: true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The tongue, continued: insults and mockery of holy things
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

rule insults
  title: Insults
  source: Sur le deuxième Commandement
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: insult_cues
  ask noul: Is a person being called insulting names here (for example 'thief', 'scoundrel', 'idiot') as an attack, and not as friendly teasing or a quotation?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.75
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label, subtitles=mute-word
  enabled: false

rule mockery_of_faith
  title: Mocking religion and holy things
  source: Sur les ennemis de notre salut
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: mockery_of_faith_cues
  ask noul: Does this make fun of religion, prayer, believers, sacred things or clergy, rather than discuss them seriously?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.75
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label, subtitles=skip-segment
  enabled: false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Detraction: Sur la Médisance and Sur le jugement téméraire
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

rule gossip
  title: Detraction and gossip
  source: Sur la Médisance
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: gossip_cues
  ask score: How much of this talks about the private faults or misdeeds of a named real person, living or dead?
    levels: none, mild, heavy
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: heavy
  action: feed-card=hide, watch-meta=warn-overlay, subtitles=skip-segment
  enabled: true

rule calumny
  title: Calumny
  source: Sur la Médisance
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: calumny_cues
  ask noul: Does this accuse a named real person of a crime or a serious fault as if it were certain, without giving any source or proof?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.85
  action: feed-card=hide, watch-meta=warn-overlay, subtitles=skip-segment
  enabled: true

rule rash_judgment
  title: Rash judgment
  source: Sur le jugement téméraire
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: rash_judgment_cues
  ask noul: Does this suggest that a named real person is guilty, lying or acting from bad motives on thin evidence (guesswork, rumour, 'body language')?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label, subtitles=skip-segment
  enabled: false

rule tale_bearing
  title: Tale-bearing
  source: Sur la Médisance
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: tale_bearing_cues
  ask noul: Does this pass on what one person said or did against another (for example 'what X said about you', leaked messages, talk behind someone's back)?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label, subtitles=skip-segment
  enabled: false

rule curiosity
  title: Curiosity about other people's affairs
  source: Sur la Pénitence
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: curiosity_cues
  ask noul: Is this title or description written to make us curious about someone's private affairs (what he said or did, what goes on inside his home or life)?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label
  enabled: false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Purity: Sur la pureté and Sur l'Impureté
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

rule impure_words
  title: Impure words and songs
  source: Sur la pureté
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: impurity_cues
  ask noul: Is this lewd talk or lewd song lyrics (sexual innuendo, sex jokes, explicit lyrics), and not sex education, medical information or news?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.75
  action: feed-card=hide, watch-meta=warn-overlay, subtitles=mute-word
  enabled: true

rule impure_sights
  title: Impure sights
  source: Sur l'Impureté
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: sexual_imagery_cues
  ask noul: Does this title or description offer nude or sexually suggestive images or scenes (for example nudity, lingerie, a 'thirst trap', an erotic dance), and not art history, medicine or news?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.75
  action: feed-card=hide, watch-meta=warn-overlay
  enabled: true

rule immodest_dress
  title: Immodest dress
  source: Sur l'Impureté
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: immodest_dress_cues
  ask noul: Is revealing or very tight clothing the attraction of this item (for example a swimwear or lingerie try-on, 'see-through', 'barely there')?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label
  enabled: false

rule familiar_company
  title: Too-familiar company between the sexes
  source: Sur l'Impureté
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: courtship_cues
  ask noul: Does this present flirting, dating or casual hookups as entertainment or advice (a dating show, pick-up tips, 'situationship' drama)?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label
  enabled: false

rule bad_books
  title: Bad books
  source: Sur la Pénitence
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: bad_books_cues
  ask noul: Is this a reading, review or promotion of a book whose selling point is lewdness or contempt for religion (erotica, 'spicy' romance, anti-religious polemic)?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label
  enabled: false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Occasions of sin: balls, shows, games, the tavern
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

rule dances
  title: Balls and dances
  source: Sur l'Impureté
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: dance_cues
  ask noul: Is this a dance party, ball or club night, or a viral dance video made for fun?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label
  enabled: false

rule spectacles
  title: Stage shows and comedies
  source: Sur la Contrition
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: spectacle_cues
  ask noul: Is this a staged show for amusement (a theatre play, comedy show, musical or circus act)?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label
  enabled: false

rule cruel_spectacles
  title: Cruel spectacles
  source: Sur le Monde
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: violence_spectacle_cues
  ask noul: Does this show or advertise people being killed, maimed or beaten for entertainment (death matches, gore, real-fight compilations)?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.75
  action: feed-card=hide, watch-meta=warn-overlay
  enabled: false

rule gambling
  title: Games played for money
  source: Sur les ennemis de notre salut
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: gambling_cues
  ask noul: Is this about gambling or betting for money (casino, poker, slots, sports betting, lottery), including tips or promotion?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.75
  action: feed-card=blank, watch-meta=warn-overlay
  enabled: false

rule drunkenness
  title: Drunkenness and the tavern
  source: Sur l'Ivrognerie
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: drunkenness_cues
  ask noul: Does this show or promote heavy drinking or getting drunk (drinking games, binge drinking, bar crawls)?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.75
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label
  enabled: false

rule gluttony
  title: Gluttony
  source: Sur la Pénitence
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: gluttony_cues
  ask noul: Does this show or promote eating far beyond need (eating challenges, mukbang, giant-portion contests)?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label
  enabled: false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Passions and other sins named in the sermons
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

rule anger
  title: Anger
  source: Sur la colère
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: anger_cues
  ask noul: Does this feature a person in a violent fit of rage (screaming, raging, meltdown), and not a calm protest or a staged scene?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label
  enabled: false

rule revenge
  title: Revenge
  source: Sur la Satisfaction
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: revenge_cues
  ask noul: Does this present taking revenge as satisfying, or urge someone to get even (revenge stories, 'petty revenge', 'make them pay')?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label, subtitles=skip-segment
  enabled: false

rule pranks
  title: Lies told to trick or amuse
  source: Sur le Mensonge
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: prank_cues
  ask noul: Is this a prank, hoax or trick in which someone is deceived for laughs?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label
  enabled: false

rule malicious_pleasure
  title: Malicious pleasure in another's misfortune
  source: Sur l'Envie
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: malicious_pleasure_cues
  ask noul: Is this made to be enjoyed as someone else's misfortune or humiliation (fails, 'karma', 'gets what he deserves')?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=dim, watch-meta=label
  enabled: false

rule divination
  title: Consulting diviners
  source: Sur la Satisfaction
  where: feed-card, watch-meta
  lexicon: divination_cues
  ask noul: Does this offer or advertise fortune-telling or divination for guidance (tarot, horoscopes, psychics, mediums)?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.75
  action: feed-card=blank, watch-meta=label
  enabled: false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Faith: Sur la religion
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

rule denial_of_god
  title: Denying that there is a God
  source: Sur la religion
  where: feed-card, watch-meta, subtitles
  lexicon: denial_of_god_cues
  ask noul: Does this state flatly that there is no God, and not just discuss atheism or the question of God's existence?
  gate: lexicon
  flag at: 0.80
  action: feed-card=blank, watch-meta=label, subtitles=skip-segment
  enabled: false
